In this case, it's meant for an update to my Hobbit patch.  Hobbits
count as small in NetHack (unlike Gnomes), which means that they
cannot wear most types of body armor.  They already get an exception
for elven mithril coats, and I added in an exception for dragon
scales, which in turn can be turned into the appropriate type of
dragon scale mail.  However, if he takes off the new suit, he won't be
able to put it back on again due to the armor limitation.  Dragon
scale mail can be made as another exception, which is what I do now,
but it doesn't make sense that a suit that would be e.g. be found on a
bones level that had belonged to a bigger race would be wearable by a
hobbit as well.

I suppose the solution would be to make objects that are small
versions of each of the suits of dragon scale mail, but I was hoping
to avoid that.

